 23%|##2       | 114/500 [00:14<00:54,  7.06it/s][['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the sum of 336695 and 349953?I think the correct answer is: 684648\n', "<think>\nTo find the sum of 336,695 and 349,953, I'll start by adding the units place. 5 plus 3 equals 8, so I'll write down 8 and move to the next place.\n\nNext, I'll add the tens place. 9 plus 5 equals 14. I'll write down 4 and carry over 1 to the hundreds place.\n\nFor the hundreds place, 6 plus 9 plus the carried-over 1 equals 16. I'll write down 6 and carry over 1 to the thousands place.\n\nIn the thousands place, 6 plus 4 plus the carried-over 1 equals 11. I'll write down 1 and carry over 1 to the ten thousands place.\n\nMoving to the ten thousands place, 3 plus 3 plus the carried-over 1 equals 7. I'll write down 7.\n\nFinally, in the hundred thousands place, there are no additional digits to add, so I'll write down 3.\n\nCombining all these results, the total sum is 686,648.\n</think>\n\nTo find the sum of **336,695** and **349,953**, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Add the units place:**\n   \\[\n   5 + 3 = 8\n   \\]\n   \n2. **Add the tens place:**\n   \\[\n   9 + 5 = 14 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 4 \\text{ and carry over } 1)\n   \\]\n   \n3. **Add the hundreds place:**\n   \\[\n   6 + 9 + 1 = 16 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 6 \\text{ and carry over } 1)\n   \\]\n   \n4. **Add the thousands place:**\n   \\[\n   6 + 4 + 1 = 11 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 1 \\text{ and carry over } 1)\n   \\]\n   \n5. **Add the ten thousands place:**\n   \\[\n   3 + 3 + 1 = 7\n   \\]\n   \n6. **Add the hundred thousands place:**\n   \\[\n   3 + 3 = 6\n   \\]\n   \nCombining all these results, the total sum is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{686,\\!648}\n\\].Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
