 29%|##9       | 145/500 [00:19<00:58,  6.04it/s][['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the sum of 292122 and 667911?I think the correct answer is: 920033\n', '<think>\nTo find the sum of 292,122 and 667,911, I will start by adding the units place. \n\n2 plus 1 equals 3, so I write down 3 in the units place.\n\nNext, I add the tens place: 2 plus 9 equals 11. I write down 1 in the tens place and carry over 1 to the hundreds place.\n\nThen, I add the hundreds place: 1 plus 7 plus the carried-over 1 equals 9. I write down 9 in the hundreds place.\n\nMoving to the thousands place: 1 plus 6 equals 7. I write down 7 in the thousands place.\n\nNext, I add the ten thousands place: 9 plus 7 equals 16. I write down 6 in the ten thousands place and carry over 1 to the hundred thousands place.\n\nFinally, I add the hundred thousands place: 2 plus 6 plus the carried-over 1 equals 9. I write down 9 in the hundred thousands place.\n\nCombining all these results, the total sum is 960,033.\n</think>\n\nTo find the sum of **292,122** and **667,911**, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Add the units place:**\n   \\[\n   2 + 1 = 3\n   \\]\n   \n2. **Add the tens place:**\n   \\[\n   2 + 9 = 11\n   \\]\n   - Write down **1** in the tens place.\n   - Carry over **1** to the hundreds place.\n\n3. **Add the hundreds place:**\n   \\[\n   1 + 7 + 1 = 9\n   \\]\n   \n4. **Add the thousands place:**\n   \\[\n   1 + 6 = 7\n   \\]\n   \n5. **Add the ten thousands place:**\n   \\[\n   9 + 7 = 16\n   \\]\n   - Write down **6** in the ten thousands place.\n   - Carry over **1** to the hundred thousands place.\n\n6. **Add the hundred thousands place:**\n   \\[\n   2 + 6 + 1 = 9\n   \\]\n\n**Final Sum:**\n\\[\n\\boxed{960,\\!033}\n\\].Therefore, my final answer is: ']]
